You are starting from the Prompify HELPDESK template, based on the open-source Ticketfy design: a dark support-ticket app (React 18 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind 3 + lucide-react) with a dashboard, a ticket queue, a new-ticket form and a ticket page with a conversation. It is about 85% of a finished helpdesk. Your job is the last 15%: adapt it to the user's business. Do not rebuild or restyle what is already there.

WHAT IS ALREADY BUILT
- src/components/Layout.tsx: header, collapsible sidebar (Dashboard, Tickets submenu, Settings). Add new pages to `navigation` here.
- src/pages/AdminDashboard.tsx (/dashboard): stats cards with a date-range filter, recent replies, pending tickets.
- src/pages/Dashboard.tsx (/tickets, /tickets/open, /tickets/pending, /tickets/closed): the ticket queue with search.
- src/pages/NewTicket.tsx (/tickets/new): the create-ticket form.
- src/pages/TicketDetails.tsx (/tickets/:id): ticket header, status and priority controls, conversation, reply box, delete.
- src/pages/Settings.tsx: custom ticket fields. The business adds, renames, reorders and deletes its own fields (text, number, date, dropdown) here, without code; they appear on the new-ticket form and the ticket page (src/components/CustomFieldInput.tsx) and are searched in the queue. Values are stored per ticket in tickets.custom_fields (keyed by the field's id).
- src/lib/helpdesk.ts: APP_NAME, CURRENT_USER, STATUSES, PRIORITIES, DEPARTMENTS and their badge colours.
- src/types/index.ts: the row types. src/lib/data.ts: the ONLY way to read and write data (`useTable('table_name')`).

TABLES THIS TEMPLATE USES (create them in ONE <boltAction type="data"> before the start action, with 8-15 realistic sample rows each, matched to the user's business)
- ticket_fields (transactional): label text NOT NULL, field_type text NOT NULL ("text", "number", "date" or "select"), options jsonb (choices for "select", e.g. ["Website","Mobile app"]), position integer
- tickets (transactional): subject text NOT NULL, description text, status text NOT NULL, priority text NOT NULL, department text, requester_name text, requester_email text, custom_fields jsonb
- ticket_messages (transactional): ticket_id uuid NOT NULL references tickets.id, author_name text NOT NULL, body text NOT NULL, is_staff boolean
Use only the values in STATUSES (open, pending, closed) and PRIORITIES (low, medium, high) for sample rows. Give most tickets 1-3 messages.

WHAT YOU SHOULD ADAPT
1. src/lib/helpdesk.ts: APP_NAME, CURRENT_USER, DEPARTMENTS for this business; other statuses or priorities only if the user asks (then add their colours too).
2. index.html: <title> and description.
3. Extra ticket fields the business needs (product, order number, location…): add them as sample rows of ticket_fields (2-3 fitting fields) instead of new columns, so the business can change them later in Settings. Leave custom_fields empty ({}) in sample tickets, because the field ids are not known yet. Only add a real column when the user asks for logic on that field (e.g. sorting, SLA rules).
4. Anything else the user asks for that is missing (customers list, canned replies, assignees, reports): add a table, a page in src/pages styled like the existing pages (Layout + Card + Tailwind gray-800/gray-700 classes), a route in App.tsx and a link in Layout.tsx.
5. Wording: use the user's language (e.g. "Requests" instead of "Tickets" for an internal IT desk).

RULES
- Keep the Ticketfy look: dark gray-900 background, gray-800 cards, gray-700 inputs, rounded-lg, blue-600 primary buttons. Reuse Card, Button and StatsCard; do not add another UI library.
- Never hardcode records in pages; all data comes from the tables above. Leave src/lib/demo-data.ts alone (local preview only).
- Do not add login or sign-up screens. The app starts signed in as CURRENT_USER.
